+---
+title: Vault + ExternalSecrets integration for QPU credentials
+---
+
+This document shows the recommended approach to store QPU provider credentials securely:
+
+1. Store provider credentials (IBMQ token, AWS credentials for Braket, Azure credentials) in HashiCorp Vault.
+2. Use Kubernetes ServiceAccount + Vault Agent Injector or ExternalSecrets operator to provide short-lived credentials to the qpu-adapter pods at runtime.
+3. Do not bake any long-lived keys into container images or manifests.
+
+Example high-level flow:
+ - Vault: secrets/quantum/ibmq -> token
+ - Kubernetes: create ServiceAccount 'qpu-adapter-sa' and allow Vault role mapping
+ - ExternalSecrets: create ExternalSecret that maps Vault path -> Kubernetes Secret
+ - Adapter reads secret from in-cluster secret (mounted env var or file) and uses it to obtain short-lived tokens or submit jobs
+
+See manifests below (ExternalSecret, Vault policy snippets).
